{
  "name": "Answer team questions in Slack from company memory with past.dev and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A Slack assistant that remembers what the team decided\n\nFor teams that answer the same questions every week: what did we decide, who promised what, is this still true.\n\n### How it works\n- One Slack Trigger receives the messages of a channel and the mentions of your bot.\n- Every message of a person goes into past.dev with its author, its time and a stable Source ID.\n- When someone mentions the bot, the AI Agent calls past.dev **Recall** as a tool, as the person who asks.\n- The agent answers in the thread and names its sources.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-hosted n8n: open **Settings > Community Nodes**, select **Install** and enter `n8n-nodes-pastdotdev` (tested with 0.1.0 on n8n 2.47). [Installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/)\n2. Create a project API key in the [past.dev console](https://app.past.dev) and add it as a **Past Dev API** credential in each past.dev node.\n3. Create a Slack app with the events `message.channels` and `app_mention`, and the scopes `channels:history`, `app_mentions:read` and `chat:write`. Add its credential, and invite the bot to the channel.\n4. In **Slack message or mention**, set the channel ID.\n5. Add your OpenAI credential.\n\n### Customization\n- Watch more channels with one Audience per private channel.\n- Ingest Linear, Jira or Notion with the same past.dev node, and the assistant answers from them too.\n",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "beb1ae53-121c-54b4-899f-d21e09c02fa4",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -800,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One trigger, two paths\nMentions go to the agent. Other messages go to memory.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "99630513-641b-569a-b99e-15c459f559b5",
      "name": "Sticky Note A",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -300,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Answer as the person who asks\nRecall returns only what this Slack user is allowed to read.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 800,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "9d270652-a8c4-5681-b114-a8c9eb44b2ca",
      "name": "Sticky Note B",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Fill the memory\nSkip bots and edits, then ingest the message with its real time.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 800,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d8d511ed-27d9-50a7-b05a-a2c4f2e003f8",
      "name": "Sticky Note C",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "trigger": [
          "message",
          "app_mention"
        ],
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "C0123456789"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "63e2f57f-e879-5267-ba39-5866fbcfb8df",
      "name": "Slack message or mention",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slackTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "7b882c9a-2b3b-55a5-bc7b-fb26c1ee85a3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "e0db5717-b2b1-5f92-bea9-b46eb0b38be7",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.type }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "rightValue": "app_mention"
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "553f19e4-80c9-5bf3-9ffe-116e6a6aa46b",
      "name": "Is it a mention?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -20,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You answer questions of the team in Slack. Today is {{ $now.toFormat('cccc d LLLL yyyy') }}.\n\nCall the tool \"Recall from past.dev\" before you answer. Answer only from what it returns. Give the date of each fact, and name the source (for example the Slack message or the document). When two facts disagree, give the most recent one and say what it replaced. If the memory does not have the answer, say so and suggest who to ask.\n\nKeep the answer short. Use Slack formatting."
        }
      },
      "id": "c54c6b23-ff69-598b-af0b-d0356d1a773a",
      "name": "Answer from company memory",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        300,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4.1-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "42a73224-a3bd-553c-91d6-3805c5609f45",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        260,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Recall what the company knows: decisions, discussions, promises, status and facts from Slack and the other connected tools. Give a precise question as the query.",
        "resource": "memory",
        "operation": "recall",
        "query": "={{ $fromAI('query', 'The question to look up in memory', 'string') }}",
        "identity": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Slack message or mention').item.json.user }}"
        },
        "options": {
          "limit": 10
        }
      },
      "id": "0ff99180-221f-53fc-9ea8-e46625226e7d",
      "name": "Recall from past.dev",
